# Nothing from the game, ever. The engine binary and its data live under
# game/, put there by setup.bat out of a copy you own; the shader dumps are
# the engine's own source, written into the working directory on every run so
# that a compile failure can be read.
game/
sdcard/
shader_*_raw.glsl
*.dds
*.brf
*.obb
*.apk
*.so
# The home-menu icon is a crop of the game's own title artwork, so it is game
# content like everything above. tools/make_icon.py rebuilds it from the copy
# under game/; without it the build falls back to libnx's default icon.
switch/icon.jpg

# Console keys are nobody's to publish, and nothing here needs them. This is
# only a guard against a stray copy in the working directory.
*.keys
keys.txt
prod.keys
title.keys

# Fetched by setup.bat, not ours to carry.
external/

# Build trees.
build/
build_switch/
build_asan/
out/

# Frame grabs, recordings and logs, written beside the executable.
*.bmp
*.wav
*.log

__pycache__/
*.pyc
